Secure version — validates the chain against the default trust store and checks the hostname:

```java
import javax.net.ssl.*;

public class SecureSocketFactory {
    public static SSLSocket createSocket(String host, int port) throws Exception {
        // Default SSLContext uses the platform trust store and validates the cert chain.
        SSLSocketFactory factory = (SSLSocketFactory) SSLSocketFactory.getDefault();
        SSLSocket socket = (SSLSocket) factory.createSocket(host, port);

        // Enforce hostname verification (not on by default for raw SSLSocket).
        SSLParameters params = socket.getSSLParameters();
        params.setEndpointIdentificationAlgorithm("HTTPS");
        socket.setSSLParameters(params);

        socket.startHandshake(); // fails fast on an invalid or mismatched certificate
        return socket;
    }
}
